blem "For the function $f(x,y),$ calculate $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}$ given that $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={y}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1+3xy).$" :question/worked-solution "To find $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{∂f}{∂y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1+3xy)) \\\\  & =3{y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1+3xy)+3x{y}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1+3xy)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382386 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124441 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "503a0bfe-7c69-5ad0-ad1d-aa8692dae673" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Expressions Involving Second-Order Partial Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ef4a7ac8-061e-5af9-9fb0-ab5773165579" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382388} {:answer/id #uuid "c4001b21-7575-5835-8086-75b8d29921b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382389} {:answer/id #uuid "5d0ca7b1-e77a-5b9b-b8a5-4b9e8d84089f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382390} {:answer/id #uuid "41d02635-e49d-571a-96b0-1ac0a22b8838" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382391} {:answer/id #uuid "6d245bf1-3343-5515-adf6-f1ffb3caa8af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382392}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d245bf1-3343-5515-adf6-f1ffb3caa8af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382392} :answer-field/id #uuid "2cf99c29-b792-5f2e-8440-d3e8129e97bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382387}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0d39e98a-42b8-56d2-88b4-63d088086c8a" :question/math-academy-id "q-80473" :question/problem "Find ${g}_{xx}(x,y)+{g}_{yy}(x,y)$ at $(1,-1)$ given that ${g}_{x}(x,y)=\\frac{2}{2x-y}$ and ${g}_{y}(x,y)=-\\frac{1}{2x-y}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find ${g}_{xx}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${g}_{x}(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({g}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{2}{2x-y}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{(2x-y)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTo find ${g}_{yy}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${g}_{y}(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{yy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({g}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-\\frac{1}{2x-y}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(2x-y)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we evaluate ${g}_{xx}(x,y)$ and ${g}_{yy}(x,y)$ at $(1,-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xx}(1,-1) & =-\\frac{4}{(2(1)-(-1))^{2}}=-\\frac{4}{9} \\\\ {g}_{yy}(1,-1) & =-\\frac{1}{(2(1)-(-1))^{2}}=-\\frac{1}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n{g}_{xx}(1,-1)+{g}_{yy}(1,-1)=-\\frac{4}{9}-\\frac{1}{9}=-\\frac{5}{9}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186422011 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124442 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "83724b66-0f15-5b94-9576-76e9dfd56d38" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Higher-Order Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c70e303-c80e-51d2-8821-2af0cf8b3950" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2y\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421995} {:answer/id #uuid "92245356-2a0e-55cd-8484-17313be9c3ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})-2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422003} {:answer/id #uuid "992b5993-493b-561e-9033-5437b3de59e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422004} {:answer/id #uuid "ca872c1a-6f89-5f8b-8336-d7cb854e1bcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x{y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422005} {:answer/id #uuid "d1afdc0c-1cf1-54cf-9c95-d81dfb59dc49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4y\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422006}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1afdc0c-1cf1-54cf-9c95-d81dfb59dc49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4y\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422006} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a95cb7d-93f6-5084-ade9-1c85a3b6b1f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422008}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fdce2d33-30de-52e0-89c4-590147a8c4ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-80479" :question/problem "Calculate ${g}_{xxy}(x,y)$ given that $g(x,y)=({x}^{2}+y)\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the first-order derivative ${g}_{x}(x,y):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(({x}^{2}+y)\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})) \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${g}_{x}(x,y)$ by differentiating ${g}_{x}(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({g}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we find ${g}_{xxy}(x,y)$ by differentiating ${g}_{xx}(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xxy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({g}_{xx}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})) \\\\  & =4y\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
